wp.html eorem for independence polynomials of claw-free graphs  [ 5 ] , both imply log-concavity in their respective settings. Root locations and coefficient questions for independence polynomials have been studied from several viewpoints; see, for example, Brown–Hickman–Nowakowski  [ 3 ] , the survey of Levit–Mandrescu  [ 20 ] , and the later work on trees and clique-cover products  [ 36 ,  37 ,  17 ] . The broader role of log-concavity in combinatorics is surveyed by Stanley  [ 31 ] , and the modern theory is also influenced by Huh’s work on chromatic and matroidal log-concavity  [ 15 ,  16 ] . 
 
 
