 Merging the five partitions’ output conjectures ( 8,281 8{,}281  in total) and removing duplicate
statements yields  6,522 6{,}522  survivors. The class-conditioned inequalities
are disjoint across partitions (each partition owns distinct target invariants on the
left-hand side), but the Sophie sufficient-conditions are not: their
consequent or antecedent is a target-independent boolean property, so different partitions might
re-derive the same condition, and removing duplicates eliminates  346 346  such cross-partition
repeats. The survivors split into  2,677 2{,}677  class-conditioned inequalities and
 3,845 3{,}845  Sophie conditions. Essentially none of the surviving novel candidates
