ial unimodality for every Z_n. Latest observed source is v1; source formulas and 2024 independent-domination counterexamples were read and distinguished. No older related campaign-summary hit found for375092/2606.04789 in the bounded local search."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r70/discovery.md", "line": 14, "text": "1. **Alikhani\u2013Peng domination-sequence unimodality**, as restated in Mohamed"}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r78/discovery.md", "line": 17, "text": "The general Alikhani\u2013Peng domination-unimodality statement was also read in Omar2601.14494v1 Conjecture1 as a preliminary lead; it was not selected or computed on."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r85/discovery.md", "line": 11, "text": "1. **Hoang\u2013Levit\u2013Mandrescu\u2013Pham connected W\u2082 criterion.** This is already excluded in r68. Independently retrieved Pereyra, arXiv:2605.14076v1; actual Theorem 5.1 and its proof say a connected W\u2082 graph is 2-quasi-regularizable iff n(G) >= 3 alpha(G), precisely the full quantified target. Theorem 4.1 is the stronger local expansion result used in its proof. Excluded as existing full proof, not a candidate. Exact cached HTML and text retained."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-fresh-source-discovery-r99/discovery.md", "line": 25, "text": "* Alikhani\u2013Ghanbari, arXiv2607.22686v1, actual HTML: definitions2.1\u20132.3 and final problems7.1\u20137.3. These concern super coalition partitions, a different invariant. A separate secondary lead to their submitted *Super domatic in graphs* was not promoted: no actual primary body or literal partition-count conjecture was obtained. No Q3-based nomination is made from that lead."}, {"path": "frontier/campaigns/2026-10-27/new-discoveries-batch2/lanes/sol-edge-irr